const comparison = `<section id="certification-vs-certificate"><h2 class="feature-title">Certification or certificate?</h2><p class="ip-section-header__lead">Choose by what you need to demonstrate, not just the name on the award.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table class="comparison"><caption>Professional certification and taught qualifications compared</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">What to compare</th><th scope="col">Professional certification</th><th scope="col">Certificate or diploma course</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Purpose</th><td>Validates professional knowledge and competence against a credentialing body's standard.</td><td>Develops and assesses learning against a course or qualification syllabus.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Typical entry</th><td>May require a degree, relevant work experience and an existing credential.</td><td>Depends on the programme; some have no formal entry requirements.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Assessment</th><td>Usually a certification examination and review of eligibility evidence.</td><td>May include exams, assignments, practical tasks or attendance requirements.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Keeping it current</th><td>Often involves renewal fees, continuing development and recertification.</td><td>The award usually records achievement at a point in time; provider rules vary.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Examples</th><td>ASP, CSP, CIH, CFPS, QEP and CIT.</td><td>NEBOSH International General Certificate, IOSH Level 3 Certificate and Level 6 diplomas.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class="fineprint page-note">A certificate of attendance is different from an assessed qualification. NEBOSH and IOSH qualifications assess learning; a course does not automatically award a professional certification. EPI is an interim designation towards QEP, not a certification. Always check the awarding body's terminology and recognition.</p></section>`;

